+
+## Direct primitive upload experiment
+
+`GOO_PRIMITIVE_UPLOAD_MODE=staged|direct` selects the primitive upload path at
+renderer creation. Staged is the default. Direct requires buffer-compatible
+`DEVICE_LOCAL | HOST_VISIBLE` memory and otherwise falls back to staging.
+Allocation, bind, and map failures remain errors. This override does not change
+text, clip, image, or path uploads.
+
+Run the focused direct-mode gate with diagnostics:
+
+```sh
+GOO_VK_DIAGNOSTICS=1 GOO_DIRECT_PRIMITIVE_UPLOAD_SMOKE=1 \
+  dotnet tests/Goo.AsyncReadbackSmoke/bin/Release/net10.0/Goo.AsyncReadbackSmoke.dll
+```
+
+The existing primitive benchmark reports requested mode, selected mode, fallback
+reason, and logical requested flush bytes alongside its CPU and GPU transfer counters. Its
+legacy `retained-primitive-staging` output prefix remains for existing parsers.
+Use `upload_mode` to identify the actual path. Direct mode remains experimental
+until paired hardware benchmarks establish its frame-time and tail-latency cost.
 
